A||||7||JohnnyK||Chucking a V6 into a 4.||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||09-25-2001||04:17 PM||||Well, I am going to throw (if I can find one cheap) a V6 into my 4 banger, and am wondering what I need. Are the mounts different? Wiring harness I assume, and the computer. Can it be a computer for a manual car from any 2.8, or does it have to be a fiero. Is there a difference between the 4 and 5 speed computers? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||09-25-2001||04:21 PM||||front motor mount, alt bracket is needed also..   <BR>(tranny mounts are the same)<P>need a computer from a 2.8 fiero or a  chip from one..    wiring harness from engine compartment.. <P>I believe the computers are different between 4-5 speeds.. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||09-25-2001||07:13 PM||||alt bracket? Wouldn't that be attached to the engine?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||09-25-2001||07:18 PM||||Fuel pump!!  This is above and beyond trying to get a few extra bucks for selling a 6 over a 4.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Elenor84||09-26-2001||01:36 AM||||Johnny man I'm doing the exact same swap...its a huge project!  If you find a cheap 6 u will need to rebuild it as I'm doing to mine...witch will cost about 1500 bucks...u have to relocate everything...fuel lines air assembly...everything!  There is to much stuff for you to buy...I suggest u buy a whole car that has a v6 in it like in a scrap yard(thats what I did) then u will have everything u need.  Just a suggestion...good luck and keep me posted.<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||pontiacs4me||09-26-2001||02:59 AM||||I did the same project back in feb.  I bought a 1985 v6 car for $250 and put all the stuff into a 87 4banger car.  I didnt rebuild the engine, it had 130K on it, but was very clean. Im thinking it may of been rebuilt, because the guy told me that the 5 or so years he owned the car he sunk $5000 into it.  So Im figuring one of those years it was probably rebuilt.  Anyway,  when you have all of the parts it only takes about 40 hours of labor to swap everything over.  I did it by myself, with the exception of 2 friends helping me shove the cradle back under the car, on a palette.    I say go for it, and if you have the money now to go v6 go L67, im doing that this winter, and I kind of wish I started off with that, because now I have to tear it all apart again.  Oh well.||||reg||1
Z||000006||pontiacs4me||09-26-2001||03:01 AM||||oh yeah one more thing.  my 87 is an auto and the 85 was a manual car.  I stuck with the auto, and just swapped engines/wiring/computer.  So I have a manual computer in an auto car and it runs fine.  But I think it idles high for an auto though.  oh well, its leaving in 4 months anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||09-26-2001||04:31 PM||||Ack! I forgot about the fuel lines and pumps. I was counting on 3-4 hours of labour (Cradle drop, new cradle in, reattach).. Crapolla.||||reg||1
